WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
Think about the last thing you bought:

2
00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.480
a sandwich, a game, a pair of sneakers.

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.050
It was worth more to you than you paid.

4
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.790
The seller got more than it cost to make.

5
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.600
Economists call those gains surplus.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.630
Millions of trades like
that happen every day.

7
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.080
Surely the market lands on
exactly the right quantity.

8
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.900
Often it doesn't.

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.280
So if buyers and sellers both gain,

10
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.840
how can a free market still
produce the wrong amount?

11
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.600
In this mission, you'll find
the quantity where marginal

12
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.880
social benefit equals
marginal social cost.

13
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.480
Then you'll calculate the deadweight
loss when a market misses that point.

14
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: find out when a
market's answer is the wrong one.
